WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Pluck a guitar string,
or blow across a flute.

2
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.720
Out comes a clear note.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.600
Keep the length fixed, and
only certain notes ever sound.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.980
The ones in between never do.

5
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.760
Set a string vibrating
in a steady pattern,

6
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.280
and watch closely.

7
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:20.500
Some points never move at all,
while others swing the most.

8
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.370
And the pattern does not
travel along the string.

9
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.350
So why only certain notes,
and never the ones in between?

10
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.810
In this mission, you'll build
a wave that stays in place,

11
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.290
from a wave and its own reflection.

12
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.160
Then you'll compare it with
a wave that moves along:

13
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.490
its energy, its amplitude and its phase.

14
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain why a string
or a flute sounds only certain notes.
